WEBVTT

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:10.502
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Jack Horton lives in San José in Costa Rica,

00:00:10.649 --> 00:00:14.208
where he teaches computer science in a secondary school.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:19.280
When he arrived in Costa Rica, the first thing that Jack noticed was

00:00:19.281 --> 00:00:21.881
how incredibly friendly the people are.

00:00:22.348 --> 00:00:25.963
Jack says the “ticos” – as they’re called in Costa Rica

00:00:26.269 --> 00:00:29.725
– are much friendlier than people in his home country.

00:00:29.904 --> 00:00:34.076
They always say <i>buenos días</i> to you even if they don’t know you.

00:00:34.736 --> 00:00:41.330
If something’s good, like a beautiful day or a good meal, the ticos say <i>pura vida</i>.

00:00:41.867 --> 00:00:44.557
It literally means “pure life.”

00:00:45.191 --> 00:00:49.232
But Jack thinks it really means “things are great.”

00:00:50.118 --> 00:00:55.415
One thing that can be difficult for foreigners is that the sense of time

00:00:55.594 --> 00:00:58.295
is completely different in Costa Rica.

00:00:58.949 --> 00:01:01.633
The Costa Ricans call it “tico time.”

00:01:02.419 --> 00:01:09.021
If there is an appointment at seven in the evening, ticos probably leave home at seven o’clock.

00:01:09.628 --> 00:01:15.540
But everyone knows it's OK not to arrive on time, and it's not a problem.

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:19.680
Another thing that surprised Jack was the weather.

00:01:20.109 --> 00:01:23.850
He thought Costa Rica was hot and sunny all the time.

00:01:24.557 --> 00:01:31.202
That’s true in the dry season, and the temperature’s about 77 degrees all year round,

00:01:31.837 --> 00:01:36.309
but in the rainy season, especially in September and October,

00:01:36.569 --> 00:01:40.444
it rains heavily for about two hours a day.

00:01:42.931 --> 00:01:47.360
Everyone told Jack that the scenery was beautiful in Costa Rica.

00:01:47.779 --> 00:01:50.760
But it was even more beautiful than he expected,

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.065
with incredible animals, birds, trees — and volcanoes.

00:01:56.529 --> 00:02:00.806
Some of the volcanoes are active and smoke quietly,

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:05.863
and then suddenly there’s a big bang and they start erupting.

00:02:06.442 --> 00:02:09.912
Jack was very frightened the first time it happened.

00:02:10.845 --> 00:02:15.282
At first, Jack thought life in Costa Rica was going to be cheap.

00:02:15.899 --> 00:02:22.430
But in fact, Jack found out that food is expensive, especially imported food.

00:02:23.211 --> 00:02:30.162
The only thing that’s cheap is fruit, vegetables, and the wonderful, wonderful coffee.

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:37.291
And the fruit and vegetables are very different from those in Jack’s home country.

00:02:37.837 --> 00:02:43.145
One day, he went to a market and he didn’t recognize any of the fruit.

00:02:43.905 --> 00:02:45.764
Jack likes San José.

00:02:46.011 --> 00:02:51.349
Some people think it can be dangerous, but Jack doesn’t feel that it is.

00:02:51.695 --> 00:02:55.307
He says it's true that some of the roads are terrible,

00:02:55.623 --> 00:02:59.428
but in general, he really loves it in Costa Rica.